{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>You shall not move your neighbor's boundary mark.</b> Rashi, of blessed memory, explained that this refers to one who moves a land-division marker backward into his fellow's field in order to widen his own. This negative commandment is included in the prohibition of theft, but Scripture comes to make him transgress two negative commandments in the land, as it says, ״בנחלתך אשר תנחל״ — in your inheritance that you inherit." "<b>And the Ramban,</b> of blessed memory, explained it as a warning not to alter the boundary of the division that the princes made when they divided the land among the tribes or among any individual of them. Therefore it says, ״אשר גבלו ראשונים״ — whom the first ones bounded — they being Elazar the priest and Joshua son of Nun and the princes of the tribes, and this is the meaning of ״בנחלתך אשר תנחל״ — in your inheritance that you inherit. And the reason for the commandment is that a person should not think to say, 'my portion is not equal to my fellow's portion because those who divided erred,' or that he might cast aspersion on the lots. Therefore He commanded that no person should dispute that division or alter the boundaries. End of quotation." "<b>And it is possible</b> to say that Scripture includes a warning against the eternity of the world (i.e., the belief in the pre-existence of the universe), for one who denies creation ex nihilo is called one who moves a boundary, for he turns backward the faith in the creation of the world, which is the boundary of the Holy One, blessed be He, who created it and delimited it at the time of His will. ״אשר גבלו ראשונים״ — whom the first ones bounded — they are the patriarchs and Moses, for the patriarchs in all their affairs and experiences testified to creation and acknowledged it, as it says (Deuteronomy 32:7): ״שאל אביך ויגדך זקינך ויאמרו לך״ — ask your father and he will tell you, your elders and they will say to you; needless to say Moses, through the truth of prophecy and the reception of the Torah. And it says, ״בנחלתך אשר תנחל״ — in your inheritance that you inherit — for the essential point and the delimited boundary in this world is your inheritance that you inherit, which is the middle of the world. And ״לא תסיג״ — you shall not move — is juxtaposed to murder, which was mentioned above, because just as moving a boundary leads to blows and murder — as it says, ״והכהו נפש״ — and he struck him fatally — and he has no refuge and no house of flight in the six cities, for they will not receive him, so too belief in pre-existence will bring a person to the death of the soul, eternal death, and his soul will not be received by the six directions corresponding to which are the six cities of refuge, as I mentioned above."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:49:35.357034561Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}